        <history>
          <p>Composed after Delius spent two years managing an orange plantation in Florida in his early twenties, this four-movement suite was his first mature orchestral work and already shows the influence of the African-American spirituals and plantation songs he heard during his time there. It went unpublished and largely unperformed publicly during his lifetime, receiving its full premiere only decades later.</p>
